 ## Install (once per computer, Windows)
 
-1. **Python with faster-whisper.** The default location is `%LOCALAPPDATA%\plaud-asr\.venv`:
+1. **Python with faster-whisper.** OpenPlod looks in `%USERPROFILE%\plaud-asr\.venv` first, then
+   `%LOCALAPPDATA%\plaud-asr\.venv`:
    ```powershell
-   py -3.12 -m venv "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\plaud-asr\.venv"
-   & "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\plaud-asr\.venv\Scripts\python.exe" -m pip install faster-whisper==1.2.1 soundfile
+   py -3.12 -m venv "$env:USERPROFILE\plaud-asr\.venv"
+   & "$env:USERPROFILE\plaud-asr\.venv\Scripts\python.exe" -m pip install faster-whisper==1.2.1 soundfile
    ```
    Then download the model once, while online, so it is in the Hugging Face cache:
    ```powershell
-   & "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\plaud-asr\.venv\Scripts\python.exe" -c "from faster_whisper import WhisperModel; WhisperModel('large-v3-turbo', device='cpu', compute_type='int8')"
+   & "$env:USERPROFILE\plaud-asr\.venv\Scripts\python.exe" -c "from faster_whisper import WhisperModel; WhisperModel('large-v3-turbo', device='cpu', compute_type='int8')"
    ```
+   **Create it from an ordinary terminal, not from inside a Microsoft Store (MSIX) app** such as the Claude
+   desktop app. Windows redirects what such an app writes under `AppData` into its own private folder
+   (`%LOCALAPPDATA%\Packages\<app>\LocalCache\...`), where OpenPlod cannot see it. That includes uv's default
+   Python folder, `%APPDATA%\uv\python`. If the venv is already there, copy the venv and the Python it was made
+   from to `%USERPROFILE%\plaud-asr\.venv` and `%USERPROFILE%\plaud-asr\python`, then change the `home =` line in
+   `.venv\pyvenv.cfg` to the new Python folder.
 2. **NeMo-Speech.cpp 0.3.0.** Download `nemo-speech-0.3.0-windows-x86_64-vulkan.zip` (GPU) and
    `nemo-speech-0.3.0-windows-x86_64-cpu.zip` from
    <https://github.com/NVIDIA/NeMo-Speech.cpp/releases/tag/v0.3.0>. Check each against that release's
